{
name = license;
value = "Google offers many fonts on open source terms. Google Sans is not one of them. Please see google.com/fonts for alternatives.";
},
{
name = note;
value = "# Round 4 — Critical notes\012\012\012* B — raised the mid crossbar slightly. Also widened slightly. Tension in the curves increased\012* C G J S — Now have perpendicular terminal endings. I would like to explore having a small angle on these **TO do!**\012* C — curve tension increased\012* D — curve tension increased slightly.\012* G — option for spurred variant. Also increased curve tension\012* E — widened\012* F – widened\012* J — widened, terminal increased and curve tension increased.\012* L — widened\012* P — widened, and counter size increased in height. Also adjusted the curve tension slightly.\012* R — Curve tension increased.\012* S — Closed terminal forms, curve tension increased\012* T — widened\012* U — Curve tension increased\012\012* a — rebalanced the form\012* b — curve tension increased, narrowed slightly.\012* c — closed terminal aperture\012* e — closed terminal aperture, curve tension increased\012* g — Closed terminal aperture, raised counter, curve tension increased\012* o — curve tension increased, narrowed slightly to be less geometric.\012* s — widened, re-balanced and closed terminal aperture\012* y — has an option for a curled ending.\012\012\012* 1 — Cap extended and made vertical\012* 2 — Terminal closed, curve tension increased\012* 3 – Terminals closed, curve tension increased\012* 5 – Terminals closed, curve tension increased\012* 6 — Terminal flattened\012* 7 — Terminal flattened\012* 9 — Terminal flattened\012\012\012* asterisk — size increase\012* hash (#) — Counter increase, widened\012* braceleft/right { } — increase in length, curve tension\012* parenleft/right ( ) — increase in height, tension\012* quotedbl “ — widened\012* cent – enlarged to cap variant, enlarged interior counters, closed terminal\012* dollar $ — updated form shape\012* € – updated form.\012* £ sterling — adjusted form, curve tension & terminal endings\012* ¥ yen — increased interior space of crossbars\012* equal – increased interior space of crossbars\012* greater / less — increased height.\012* ~ asciitilde — increased terminals\012* & ampersand — form change, curve tension and terminal ends\012* copyright / registered – size increase,\012* trademark – size increase";
},
{
name = Axes;
value = (
{
Name = Weight;
Tag = wght;
},
{
Name = "Optical size";
Tag = opsz;
}
);
}
);
